 "text": "9/29/26, 9:39 AM\n\nYou can change the date of a move-in after it has been created without affecting the move-out that precedes it. To do this, choose\nEdit\u00bb Change Move-In Date\n\nActual Move-In Date\nIn addition to the move-in date, the actual move-in date can be entered as the date from which the premise is occupied.\nSave\n\nWhen you save the move-in, the initial move-in or move-in/out screen reappears. In Customizing under Define Control Parameters\nat Document Level, you can configure the system so that when you save the data, a log is displayed containing information on the\nchanges made to the data.\n\nCertain move-in activities, for example, maintaining a budget billing plan, are based on the database changes made by the move-in.\nIn these instances, you can, in Customizing under Move-In/Out -> Move-In -> Define Control Parameters at Document Level\nconfigure the system to either output a confirmation prompt or save the data automatically before the action is carried out.\n\nYou can also save your changes in the move-in without leaving the move-in screen. To do this, choose Save and Hold.\n\nMaster Data (Move-In)\n\nUse\n\nDuring move-in processing, one or more contracts are created to commence on the specified move-in date. The installations you\nspecified at the start of processing are allocated to these contracts.\n\nIf the move-in date is in a period in which one of the installations has already been billed then the move-in cannot be created.\n\nYou can save changes to business partner and contract account data as scheduled changes. This means that the changes are not\nactivated until a future date. This date is determined by subtracting the interval period defined in Customizing from the move-in\ndate. For more information on how to define the interval period, see Customizing under |)*SAP Utilities Customer Service\n\nProcess Execution } Move-In/Move-Out \u00bb Define System Parameters for Move-in and Move-Out 3). Scheduled changes are\nactivated by report BUSPCDACT (activation of scheduled change documents for an application object).\n\nWhen a move-in is created, the tax jurisdiction code of the connection object address is copied to all the contracts of the move-in\ndocument, as well as to all the business partner addresses that were automatically created through the move-in.\n\nStandard Business Partner Address\n\nIn Customizing (|}#SAP Utilities \u00bb Customer Service \u00bb Process Execution \u00bb Move-In/Out \u00bb Move-In \u00bb Define Move-In Control\nParameters at Document Level | ), you can configure the system so that the business partner receives the address of the premise\nhe/she is moving into as the default address. If you want to process the move-in for different premises in one move-in document,\nthe system uses the premise address of the installation that was entered first.\n\nYou can find additional information in the section on the master data component.\n\nUsing the Business Add-In (Badl) ISU_LMOVEIN_SETBPADDR, you can allocate a default value to the standard address.\n\nMatar Raadino Nata (Mavea-ln)\n",
